     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults in a hospital, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the typical maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially.\n\nCould you confirm what was intended? Some common options are:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total), which may be what was meant.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for adults.\n\nOnce you tell me the dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. If 1,600 mg four times daily really is what you want, tell me and I'll add a note on the order with your rationale. I'd still recommend a pharmacist review first."
      }
     ],
